# Tests

Assert the new behavior. Do not re-assert contracts another test already covers.

`done()` after `next()` on the last prayer, with `current()` still that prayer, is already tested. A new field on `current()` inherits it — do not check `done()`, the last `key`, or `reset()` in that field’s test.

```js
// Good — index is 1-based and runs 1…total
assert.deepStrictEqual(
  collectSteps(r).map(step => step.index),
  Array.from({ length: r.total }, (_, i) => i + 1),
)

// Not — done(), last key, and reset are other tests
assert.strictEqual(r.current().key, 'creed')
assert.ok(r.done())
r.reset()
assert.strictEqual(r.current().index, 1)
```

When an existing `deepStrictEqual` on `current()` would fail, add the new field there. Do not add a second full-object assertion.
